WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.617 --> 00:00:18.058
and Mandy were glad when the twins left.

2
00:00:19.259 --> 00:00:22.240
But two minutes later, Mom brought bad news.

3
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:26.362
"Get changed," Mom said excitedly.

4
00:00:26.382 --> 00:00:29.583
"We're going to an art gallery!"

5
00:00:29.603 --> 00:00:34.706
"What?" Vinnie and Mandy said together.

6
00:00:34.726 --> 00:00:38.469
"It's at the college," said Mom.

7
00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:41.751
"It'll be a good experience for you."

8
00:00:41.771 --> 00:00:46.535
"But, Mom Mandy cried.

9
00:00:46.555 --> 00:00:50.578
"I don't want to go," said Vinnie.

10
00:00:52.199 --> 00:00:54.301
Mom gave them a long stare.

11
00:00:56.002 --> 00:00:57.724
The children knew what that meant.

12
00:00:59.236 --> 00:01:02.839
Vinnie and Mandy went up the stairs, dragging their feet.

13
00:01:02.859 --> 00:01:06.102
"I can't believe this.

14
00:01:06.762 --> 00:01:11.446
I don't want to go to a boring art gallery," said Vinnie.

15
00:01:11.466 --> 00:01:18.652
"Well, it might be fun," said Mandy, trying to sound cheerful.

16
00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:23.576
The children reluctantly went to their bedrooms to get dressed.

17
00:01:25.008 --> 00:01:29.572
Vinnie was combing his hair in front of the mirror when Mandy knocked on his door.

18
00:01:29.592 --> 00:01:31.954
"Are you ready?"

19
00:01:32.714 --> 00:01:34.316
she asked when he opened the door.

20
00:01:35.897 --> 00:01:38.079
Vinnie quickly pulled her into his room.

21
00:01:38.099 --> 00:01:42.682
"Hey, we have some time," he said.

22
00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:46.966
"Why don't we go on a trip before leaving?"

23
00:01:46.986 --> 00:01:54.652
"Okay, then at least something exciting will happen this afternoon," agreed Mandy.

24
00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.141
The children ran up to the attic.

25
00:01:59.542 --> 00:02:01.763
The album was still on the bookshelf.

26
00:02:03.403 --> 00:02:04.124
"Open it!"

27
00:02:04.944 --> 00:02:05.664
urged Vinnie.

28
00:02:05.684 --> 00:02:09.646
"Kids! We're leaving in one minute!"

29
00:02:10.627 --> 00:02:11.427
shouted Mom.

30
00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:14.268
Mandy opened the album.

31
00:02:15.629 --> 00:02:20.511
In the next photo, the old man was standing with some people beside a table.

32
00:02:21.892 --> 00:02:25.878
On the table was an object that looked like a little tree.

33
00:02:27.378 --> 00:02:30.480
But all the branches formed a perfect egg shape.

34
00:02:32.021 --> 00:02:34.903
Light glowed from inside an opening at the top.

35
00:02:34.923 --> 00:02:37.344
"What's that?

36
00:02:37.904 --> 00:02:39.925
Is it a tree or an egg?"

37
00:02:40.846 --> 00:02:41.766
whispered Mandy.

38
00:02:41.786 --> 00:02:44.988
"I'm not going to call you again!"

39
00:02:46.909 --> 00:02:49.230
They heard Mom's footsteps on the stairs.

40
00:02:50.331 --> 00:02:51.892
She did not sound happy.

41
00:02:53.564 --> 00:02:55.585
Vinnie and Mandy looked at each other.

42
00:02:57.246 --> 00:02:59.106
Mom's footsteps got closer.

43
00:03:00.687 --> 00:03:06.049
Just as she flung open the attic door, Vinnie and Mandy started down the dark tunnel.

44
00:03:09.991 --> 00:03:14.513
The last thing they saw was their mom standing in the doorway, looking stunned.

45
00:03:16.214 --> 00:03:17.554
Mandy fell first.

46
00:03:18.995 --> 00:03:21.576
She landed hard on a wooden surface.

47
00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.501
Vinnie fell nearby.

48
00:03:26.062 --> 00:03:30.404
They were in a large space with thick, dark curtains in front of them.

49
00:03:32.005 --> 00:03:34.967
Behind them was beautifully painted scenery.

50
00:03:36.828 --> 00:03:42.151
Through a small opening where the curtains met, the children could see bright lights.

51
00:03:43.712 --> 00:03:45.193
They heard loud clapping.

52
00:03:45.213 --> 00:03:48.635
"It's so noisy!"

53
00:03:49.275 --> 00:03:50.096
shouted Vinnie.

54
00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.021
He peeked between the curtains.

55
00:03:53.041 --> 00:03:57.262
"Uh-oh!" he cried.

56
00:03:59.002 --> 00:04:03.524
The applause got louder, and suddenly, the curtain began to open.

57
00:04:05.364 --> 00:04:07.585
Vinnie and Mandy were on a stage!

58
00:04:09.305 --> 00:04:14.167
Vinnie grabbed his sister's hand and quickly dragged her to the side of the stage.

59
00:04:15.827 --> 00:04:17.448
Loud applause broke out.

60
00:04:19.024 --> 00:04:21.765
"Bravo! Bravo!"

61
00:04:22.666 --> 00:04:23.846
the audience cheered.

62
00:04:25.667 --> 00:04:28.168
Vinnie and Mandy watched the opening curtain.

63
00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:32.870
The crowd was standing up, shouting and clapping.

64
00:04:34.571 --> 00:04:39.473
A beautiful dancer was at the front of the stage, bowing and blowing kisses.

65
00:04:41.574 --> 00:04:45.296
The audience was throwing roses at their favorite ballerina.
